---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const counted = Boolean(site.analyticsToken);
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this site collects, and what it does not.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>What this site collects</h1>
      <p class="lead">Very little, and nothing to track you.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      {counted ? (
        <>
          <h2>No cookies, no tracking</h2>
          <p>
            This site sets no cookies and runs no advertising or tracking scripts. It counts visits without identifying
            you, as described below. Its fonts are served from this site, not from a third party.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <h2>No tracking</h2>
          <p>
            This site sets no cookies and runs no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts. Its fonts are served from
            this site, not from a third party.
          </p>
        </>
      )}

      {counted && (
        <>
          <h2>Visit counts</h2>
          <p>
            We count visits with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, to
            learn which pages are read and how quickly they load. When a page opens, your browser sends Cloudflare the
            page address, the site that linked to it, its user agent (which names the browser, operating system and type
            of device) and page loading times. Like any web request, this reaches Cloudflare with your IP address, from
            which Cloudflare works out the country. We see only totals.
          </p>
          <p>
            The counter stores nothing on your device.{' '}
            <a href="https://blog.cloudflare.com/free-privacy-first-analytics-for-a-better-web/">Cloudflare states</a>{' '}
            that it uses no cookies or local storage to track visitors and does not fingerprint them by IP address, user
            agent or any other data. Its handling is described in the{' '}
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>. Content blockers that
            block <code>static.cloudflareinsights.com</code> stop the count entirely, and the site works the same.
          </p>
        </>
      )}

      <h2>Your theme choice</h2>
      <p>
        If you switch between light and dark, the choice is stored in your own browser so the next page opens the same
        way. It never leaves your device.
      </p>

      <h2>The contact form</h2>
      <p>
        What you enter in the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> (your name, email address, organisation, topic and
        message and, if you ask about early access, what you tell us about your work and compute) is delivered to us
        through <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree</a>, which processes it on our behalf.
        Like any web request, it reaches Formspree with your IP address and the name of your browser. We use it only to
        reply to you and to follow up on what you asked about. We do not sell it or share it with anyone else. Please
        leave out anything confidential or unpublished.
      </p>
      <p>
        With JavaScript turned off in your browser, the form is sent as a plain web form, and Formspree then shows its
        own confirmation page, which sets a cookie of Formspree's and loads Google Tag Manager, under Formspree's
        privacy policy. With JavaScript on, as usual, you stay on this site.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use these details because you asked us to: without them we cannot answer you or, for early access or a study,
        take the steps you asked for before any agreement. Formspree sends your message to {site.email}, which reaches
        our mailbox through Cloudflare's email routing, and keeps a copy in our Formspree account. These services may
        process it outside your country, including in the United States.
      </p>
      <p>We keep messages only as long as we need them for what you asked.</p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          GitHub Pages
        </a>
        , which records the IP addresses of visitors for security, as described in its own privacy statement.
      </p>

      <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not track visitors across sites, so it treats every visit the same way whether or not your
        browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        To see, correct or delete what you have sent us, or to object to how we use it, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. If you are in the European Union or the United Kingdom, you
        can also complain to your data protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change what this site collects, we will update this page and the date below.</p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated September 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .updated {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--fg-subtle);
  }
</style>
